{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Tune: the drawer's small corrections.

  NO "YOU SAVED (57%)" ROW. pg-cart-total renders the summary block as
  Subtotal / Extra 10% Off / You saved (n%), and the theme's own Total sits
  right beneath it. Per the owner the saved line comes out: the discount rows
  above it already say what came off, and repeating it as a percentage next to
  the real total is noise at the moment of paying. Only that row is hidden —
  Subtotal and Extra 10% Off stay, and pg-cart-total keeps computing the block,
  so nothing downstream of it changes.

  A BIGGER SHIPPING PROTECTION ROW, THE SAME HEIGHT. In the sticky panel the
  row is shrunk hard (title 12.5px, sub 10.5px, price 12.5px) and reads as fine
  print next to the checkout button. Each is stepped up ~1px and the line
  heights and paddings are tightened by the same amount, so the box occupies
  the same space it does today: the panel is sticky and every pixel added there
  pushes the checkout button down.

  THE UPSELL ROW STOPS EATING THE DRAWER. nc-cro's recommendation rows put the
  product name on as many lines as it wants and drop the SAVE % chip onto a line
  of its own, so one upsell ran several lines deep in a drawer that has to show
  the cart as well. The name is now one line with an ellipsis, and the chip is
  inline beside the price where it belongs. The row's own padding is trimmed a
  couple of pixels with it.

  The title's element is not the same on every row (the markup comes from
  nc-cro), so the nowrap rule lists the candidates it can be rather than
  guessing one — anything not present simply matches nothing.

  THE TOP OF THE DRAWER: THE WHITE BAND AND THE FAINT RULES. Three things stack
  above the first cart line, and two of them are hairlines the owner could see
  and not name. Read off the sections that draw them:

    - pg-drawer's .pg-cart-top is the sticky "Your Cart" header, and it carries
      `border-bottom:1px solid rgba(122,47,162,.16)` -- a faint PURPLE rule;
    - nc-cartfix's .nc-drawer-top is the logo + "Free shipping on every order"
      block, `padding:2px 0 14px`, `margin:0 0 8px`, and its own
      `border-bottom:1px solid rgba(15,42,51,.08)` sitting directly under that
      pill -- the second rule, and the band of empty white between them.

  Both borders come off and the block is compressed: 14px of bottom pad to 6px,
  8px of margin to 4px, and the logo's own 12px bottom margin to 7px. Roughly
  25px comes back at the top of the drawer with nothing removed from it. The
  upsell block's heading and note are trimmed with them, being the next tallest
  thing above the cart itself. .pg-bar's border stays: that one outlines the
  free-shipping progress card, so it reads as a box rather than a stray line.

  THE FREE GIFT LINE'S SAVE %. By request the gift reads like every other line:
  $13.99 struck, $0.00 charged, and the percentage in the price corner beneath
  them. The struck pair is already there -- .nc-lsave renders it from the
  variant's compare-at, which is set on the product -- but the percentage was
  not, and could not be:

    - pg-drawer's pgDeals, which builds .pg-save-chip, returns early on any row
      whose link contains 'free-gift', so no chip is ever created on that line;
    - pg-drawer then hides .pg-save-chip on it as well, so un-hiding an element
      that does not exist changes nothing (that rule is dropped here);
    - pg-chips DOES reach the row, but writes the word FREE into a chip it finds
      rather than creating one.

  So a chip of its own is added: .pg-gift-off, mounted inside .nc-lsave so it
  lands in the price column under the two figures. Its own class is the point --
  nothing else in the theme writes it, so there is no second writer to race, and
  the ping-pong that made the add-on label flicker cannot repeat here. It is
  mounted only when it is missing or not already last in its host, so a settled
  line is left untouched; when .nc-lsave has not rendered it falls back inside
  the title's h2, which is a cell the grid already owns, rather than becoming a
  loose grid item that lands in someone else's column.

  THE FREE GIFT PILL, LEFT. It is pulled to the left edge of its line, under
  the product title. pg-drawer's ftFix() writes an inline text-indent and width
  on it from a measurement taken before the webfont settles, and inline
  !important cannot be beaten from a stylesheet — but with the pill's own box
  restated here it lands correctly as soon as ftFix is not fighting it.

  WHY pg-gift-fix IS GONE. It added the free case itself. So does pg-giftguard,
  which already owned that job — pg-drawer's own giftSync was disabled in favour
  of it, with a comment saying exactly why: "re-enabling this add would mean TWO
  owners racing to add the same gift and a cart that intermittently holds two of
  them. One owner." pg-gift-fix made a third owner, on its own clock, each
  refreshing the drawer after its own add. That is the cart glitching, and the
  second case. Deleted, not patched — the gift needs one owner and it already
  has one.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* the saved-percent row in the drawer's total block */
  #cart .pg-tot-r.pg-tot-saved,
  body.template-cart .pg-tot-r.pg-tot-saved{display:none !important}

  /* shipping protection: larger type, same box */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp{padding:6px 10px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t b{font-size:13.5px !important;line-height:1.2 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t small{font-size:11.5px !important;line-height:1.2 !important;margin-top:0 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-price{font-size:13.5px !important}
  /* outside the sticky panel (cart page, drawer body) it is already roomier —
     nudge the same amount without touching the padding */
  #cart .pg-sp-t b{font-size:14px}
  #cart .pg-sp-t small{font-size:12px;line-height:1.25}
  #cart .pg-sp-price{font-size:14px}

  /* the in-cart upsell rows: one-line name, chip beside the price, less height */
  #cart .nc-rec{padding-top:7px !important;padding-bottom:7px !important}
  #cart .nc-rec-info{min-width:0 !important}
  #cart .nc-rec-info > h3,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > h4,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > b,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > a,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > .nc-rec-t,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > .nc-rec-title,
  #cart .nc-rec-t,
  #cart .nc-rec-title{
    display:block !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
    overflow:hidden !important;
    text-overflow:ellipsis !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
  }
  #cart .nc-rec-price,
  #cart .nc-rec-was,
  #cart .nc-rec-off{display:inline-block !important;vertical-align:middle !important}
  #cart .nc-rec-off{margin-left:8px !important;padding:2px 8px !important;line-height:1.4 !important}

  /* no hairline above or below the free-shipping pill, and less air with it;
     the upsell block's heading + note are the next tallest thing above the cart */
  #cart .nc-drawer-top{padding:0 0 6px !important;margin:0 0 4px !important;border-bottom:0 !important}
  #cart .nc-dlogo,#cart .nc-dlogo-txt{margin-bottom:7px !important}
  #cart .pg-cart-top{border-bottom:0 !important;padding-top:9px !important;padding-bottom:9px !important}
  #cart .cart-upsell h3{font-size:14px !important;margin:0 0 2px !important}
  #cart .nc-upsell-note{font-size:11px !important;padding:4px 10px !important;margin:2px 0 7px !important}
  #cart .nc-recs,
  #cart .nc-recs-panel{margin-top:2px !important}

  /* the FREE GIFT pill sits at the left edge of its line, under the title */
  #cart .pg-free-tag,
  body.template-cart .pg-free-tag{
    width:max-content !important;
    text-indent:0 !important;
    padding:6px 12px !important;
    text-align:left !important;
    justify-self:start !important;
    align-self:start !important;
    margin-left:0 !important;
    margin-right:auto !important;
  }
  /* and the gift line gets its own percentage, in the price corner under the
     struck $13.99 and the $0.00 -- geometry and colour matched to .pg-save-chip
     so the two read as the same badge on different rows */
  #cart .pg-gift-off,
  body.template-cart .pg-gift-off{
    display:inline-flex !important;align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important;
    background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4 0%,#7A2FA2 30%,#4A1C66 50%,#7A2FA2 70%,#9B4BC4 100%);
    background-size:240% 240%;animation:pgShift 5s ease-in-out infinite;
    color:#fff !important;-webkit-text-fill-color:#fff !important;
    font-size:12px !important;font-weight:700 !important;line-height:1 !important;
    letter-spacing:normal !important;word-spacing:normal !important;text-indent:0 !important;
    padding:6px 7px !important;border-radius:999px !important;
    width:fit-content !important;max-width:100% !important;min-width:0 !important;flex:none !important;
    margin:2px 0 0 !important;
  }

  /* --- the upsell row on the two phones that matter ---
     iPhone 13/14/16/17 report a 390-393px viewport, the Pro Max models 430-440.
     The row has to fit picture + one-line name + price + chip + ADD in both, so
     the small class steps everything down a point and shrinks the thumbnail,
     and the large class takes the middle size rather than the desktop one. */
  @media (max-width:400px){
    #cart .nc-rec{gap:8px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec img{width:52px !important;height:52px !important;flex:0 0 52px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-t,
    #cart .nc-rec-title{font-size:13px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-price{font-size:13.5px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-was{font-size:11.5px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-off{font-size:10.5px !important;margin-left:6px !important;padding:2px 6px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-add{padding:7px 12px !important;font-size:11.5px !important}
  }
  @media (min-width:401px) and (max-width:480px){
    #cart .nc-rec img{width:58px !important;height:58px !important;flex:0 0 58px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-t,
    #cart .nc-rec-title{font-size:13.5px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-price{font-size:14px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-was{font-size:12px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-off{font-size:11px !important;margin-left:7px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-add{padding:8px 14px !important;font-size:12px !important}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgGiftOff) return; window.pgGiftOff = 1;

  function giftRows(){
    var out = [];
    document.querySelectorAll('#cart .l4ca > li, body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca > li')
      .forEach(function(li){ if (li.querySelector('.pg-free-tag')) out.push(li); });
    return out;
  }

  function pass(){
    giftRows().forEach(function(li){
      /* the price column when it has rendered, the title's own cell otherwise --
         never a loose grid item, see the note above */
      var host = li.querySelector('.nc-lsave') || li.querySelector('h2');
      if (!host) return;
      var chip = li.querySelector('.pg-gift-off');
      if (!chip){
        chip = document.createElement('span');
        chip.className = 'pg-gift-off';
        chip.textContent = '-100%';
      }
      /* settle, do not fight: a chip already sitting last in its host is left
         alone, so this writes nothing on the passes after the first */
      if (chip.parentNode !== host || chip !== host.lastElementChild) host.appendChild(chip);
    });
  }

  var pending = false;
  function soon(){
    if (pending) return;
    pending = true;
    setTimeout(function(){ pending = false; pass(); }, 80);
  }

  if (window.MutationObserver){
    (function watch(){
      var c = document.getElementById('cart');
      if (c){ try { new MutationObserver(soon).observe(c, {childList:true, subtree:true}); } catch(e){} }
      else setTimeout(watch, 500);
    })();
  }
  setInterval(pass, 1200);
  pass();
})();
</script>
